me Esper story and  at the helm of everything is generic  background looking character mob who  holds the entire series together through  being the definition of chill his  calmness and ability to take on  seemingly any situation is integral in  keeping the series grounded because it  does get incredibly crazy at times but  having mob stops it all from moving too  far into the realm of abstract and mob  is just a fantastic character in his own  right as well this is not something that  will become apparent immediately but mob  has a serious character arc going  through this short but sweet story and  it's a big WOW moment when you look back  on where he came from  after seeing where he ends up he's far  from the emotionless derp he appears to  be and it was a pleasure to follow his  journey of change however my personal  favorite character in the series would  have to be breakin one of our secondary  protagonists from the very first episode  this man is pure hilarity and a lot of  that comes from the brilliant vocal  performance of takahiro sakurai  a man  I know best Isuzu crew from koteas and  my god is this a different role Regan is  a true force to behold on screen  confidently weaving his way around the  world of psychic powers that he has no  business being in whatsoever and just  like mob he's not a one-note character  either and is capable of superb drama  and strangely enough given that he is  into nespa even the odd dose of action  and the rest of the cast really do  embody that as well because no one is  really who they seem upon being  introduced mob psycho 100 really enjoys  playing with anime tropes specifically  in regards to characterization and as a  result you can never really predict the  twists and turns of certain individuals  will take and one really simple example  of this would be very early on in the  series where we have a super  intimidating group of muscle heads  introduced known as the body Improvement  Club and they're introduced to us 